Actually, it isn't in the same league -- as you pointed out, it confirms
overeating.  It should confirm all such stupid deaths or none.

Related:  I'd like to see a "runstop" option, where you stop any time you
come upon anything "interesting" -- e.g., running down a corridor you now
go right past doors; running through a dark room (to get an idea of its size)
you go right past piles of money, etc., unless they're directly in your
path.  Since you _see_ things in adjacent squares, you ought to have the
option of stopping & dealing with them.  (Of course, this only becomes really
annoying on a dark "big room" level. . .)


Some objects to add:

Spellbooks of fairly useless spells.  E.g., "confuse self."
Statuary shops.  (If you start pickaxing unpaid-for statues, the owner
	will expect payment!)
Trap components.  Perhaps this would be something that rogues had an
	intrinsic ability (at some level) to use.  Also, the ability to
	"steal" the components for a detected trap, at a percent chance
	of setting it off (lower percent for rogues).  Obvious exception:
	you can't "steal" the components of pits and trapdoors.  (Duuuuh.)

